# 365Signal Agent v0.4 — Collaborative Writing & Editorial Agent

## Mission

Extend the existing 365Signal Agent v0.3 application on Ubuntu with a collaborative AI Writing Agent.

**The objective is to move from autonomous draft generation to human-directed editorial collaboration.**

The Research Agent discovers and analyses Microsoft security developments autonomously. The Writing Agent transforms that research into original, technically credible commentary, then collaborates interactively with the human author to develop, challenge, revise and finalise articles.

The intended experience should resemble an author working with a research assistant and professional editor, not an automated content-generation tool.

Do not rebuild the application. Extend the existing architecture.

## Existing capabilities

365Signal v0.3 has demonstrated:

- LinkedIn OAuth and API integration.
- Local Qwen inference through LM Studio.
- Autonomous discovery across 14 configured research sources.
- Article deduplication and development analysis.
- Weighted ranking of security developments.
- Autonomous topic selection.
- LinkedIn draft generation.
- Separate editorial validation.
- SQLite research persistence.
- Research reporting and audit records.
- Human approval and cancellation workflows.

