# 1. Required outcome

At the end of v0.4, the operator must be able to:

1. Open an existing research development or generated draft.
2. Ask the Writing Agent to propose an original editorial argument.
3. Review the proposed thesis and supporting evidence.
4. Ask the agent to generate a structured outline.
5. Generate an initial draft.
6. Edit the draft conversationally using natural-language instructions.
7. Preserve selected paragraphs while revising others.
8. Compare versions and restore an earlier draft.
9. Challenge factual claims and request stronger evidence.
10. Submit the chosen revision for editorial validation.
11. Approve the final version for the existing LinkedIn publication workflow.

The author retains editorial authority throughout.

The Writing Agent must not publish autonomously.

