# 4. Editorial workspace

Provide an operator-friendly editing interface using the application's existing UI conventions.

If no suitable UI exists, implement a minimal CLI-based conversational workspace first.

Do not build a large web application simply to satisfy this sprint.

The interface must allow the author to:

- List research developments.
- Open an existing research brief.
- Create a writing session.
- Review proposed angles.
- Select or modify an angle.
- Generate and read a draft.
- Submit revision instructions.
- Inspect version history.
- Compare revisions.
- Restore a previous version.
- Request editorial review.
- Mark a final draft as ready for approval.

A suggested CLI workflow is:

`365signal write start --development <id>`

`365signal write angles --session <id>`

`365signal write draft --session <id>`

`365signal write revise --session <id>`

`365signal write history --session <id>`

`365signal write diff --session <id> --from 1 --to 2`

`365signal write review --session <id>`

These are illustrative commands. Follow the repository's existing conventions.

