# 5. Editorial version control

Implement durable writing sessions.

Suggested logical entities:

### WritingSession

- Session ID
- Research development ID
- Selected editorial angle
- Intended audience
- Content format
- Creation and modification timestamps
- Current draft version
- Session status

### DraftVersion

- Version ID
- Session ID
- Version number
- Complete draft content
- Parent version
- Revision instruction
- Created timestamp
- Editorial status
- Supporting source references

### EditorialReview

- Review ID
- Draft version ID
- Validator version
- Evidence references
- Findings
- Verdict
- Revision recommendations
- Timestamp

Use the existing SQLite database and migration conventions where appropriate.

Draft versions must be immutable.

Store the full text for every committed version.

Allow operators to inspect previous versions without reconstructing them from model output.

Maintain an audit record of revisions, reviews and approvals.

