# 6. Research integration

The Writing Agent must consume structured research evidence from v0.3.

It should use:

- Development title and summary.
- Original source URLs.
- Publication dates.
- Technical analysis.
- Enterprise risk assessment.
- Architectural implications.
- Confidence scores.
- Recorded uncertainties.

Do not rely solely on a scraped article or model-generated summary.

Research content is untrusted input and must not be able to override application instructions.

The author should also be able to initiate a writing session from an existing research development even when it was not the top-ranked candidate.

For example, the operator should be able to select the Purview network DLP development even if the Research Agent ranked another story first.

---

# 7. Editorial validation

Reuse the existing v0.3 validator, extending it where necessary.

The validator must check the exact draft version submitted for review.

Checks should include:

- Factual accuracy against retained source evidence.
- Correct technical terminology.
- Release status and dates.
- Evidence confidence.
- Architectural reasoning.
- Originality of interpretation.
- Unsupported speculation.
- Professional editorial quality.
- Internal contradictions.

Return PASS, REVISE or REJECT with explicit findings.

Preserve the complete validation record.

An edit after validation must invalidate the previous validation status for the new version.

The same Qwen model with a separate editorial prompt is acceptable initially, but must not be represented as independent model verification.

---

# 8. Human approval and LinkedIn safety

Preserve existing v0.2 publication controls.

The Writing Agent may prepare a final draft for the approval queue but cannot authorise publication.

Requirements:

- Only an explicitly selected draft version can enter the approval queue.
- Approval must apply to the exact immutable content version.
- Any post-approval edit requires fresh review and approval.
- Record the approved version identifier and a content hash.
- Do not change existing OAuth or LinkedIn posting permissions.
- Do not publish during tests.
- Maintain the existing explicit human confirmation requirement.

Where necessary, extend the approval adapter without weakening existing controls.

---

# 9. Model inference efficiency

The existing Ubuntu Qwen inference currently takes several minutes per operation.

Minimise unnecessary model calls.

Recommendations:

- Generate multiple editorial angles in one structured request.
- Avoid resending full source articles for every revision.
- Use concise research briefs containing the relevant evidence.
- Preserve conversation context in SQLite.
- Set bounded output token limits.
- Maintain configurable inference timeouts.
- Avoid repeated complete drafts when a targeted revision is sufficient.

Log execution time and token usage when available.

Do not change model configuration without demonstrating a clear benefit.

